{
  "id": "jar-rack-tall",
  "name": "Jar rack - tall jars (2 tiers)",
  "comment": "Slide-in jar rack for the garage shelf: 411 x 730 x 226, for the 150-high jars (Ø90). Stacked columns: each side is one 18 mm piece per tier (158 high, then a 50 lip strip) stacked in one plane with the full-width shelves 411 x 727 between them (bottom faces at 158), each shelf resting on the side pieces below along its whole length. Each shelf is tied to the side pieces under it by four 20x20x40 angle brackets (2 mm sheet, four 3.5x16 screws) in the top corners of the tier below, front and back, in the headroom over the jars; the lip strips are screwed down into the top shelf with three 5x70 wood screws each. The load goes down through the boards; the brackets and screws only hold position. Built top-down, upside down on the bench. No bottom (the deck is the first floor), no top, 3 mm HDF back stapled over every rear edge. Tiers of 158 / 158 clear; the top tier's jars reach 326 (entrance 350). 4 jars across x 8 deep = 32 per tier, 64 in the module. Generated by scripts/gen-jar-rack.mjs.",
  "buildable": true,
  "color": "#ffffff",
